 inconsistencies in datasets and baselines in previous research, as noted by  \cite{formanek2024dispelling}, we select two of the most well-evaluated benchmarks, the \texttt{MPE} and 2-agent \texttt{HalfCheetah} datasets provided by OMAR \cite{pan2022plan},  and the \texttt{MaMuJoCo} datasets provided by OG-MARL \cite{formanek2023off} and MADiff \cite{zhu2024madiff}. OMAR provides four-level datasets: Expert, Medium, Medium-Replay, and Random, while OG-MARL provides three: Good, Medium, and Poor. All offline datasets are open-sourced\footnote{OMAR datasets: \url{https://github.com/ling-pan/OMAR}} \footnote{OG-MARL datasets: \url{https://github.com/instadeepai/og-marl}}.


