$\,\, \pi_D(x_1, d | x_2) \propto u_D(x_1,d)p_D(x_2|x_1)p_D(x_1) $
and use the fact that $d^{*}(x_2) = \\\text{mode}_{d}(\pi_D(x_1, d | x_2 ))$, to solve the problem with one APS, again defined using only the original terms in the ID. %
