\title{Linearization via Rewriting}
\author{Ugo dal Lago and Federico Olimpieri}

\begin{document}

\maketitle

\begin{abstract}
	We introduce the \emph{structural resource $\lambda$-calculus}, a new 
	formalism in which strongly normalizing terms of the $\lambda$-calculus can  
	naturally be represented, and at the same time any type derivation can be 
	internally rewritten to its linearization. The calculus is shown to be 
	normalizing and confluent. Noticeably, \emph{every} strongly normalizable 
	$\lambda$-term can be represented by a type derivation. This is the first example 
	of a system where the linearization process takes place \emph{internally}, while remaining 
	purely \emph{finitary} and \emph{rewrite-based}.
\end{abstract}

