\textbf{(The Skilled Team Search in Collaboration Social Network)} 
To accomplish a new project, a manager wants to recruit an experienced team that consists of members with relevant skills and previous collaboration experiences. Figure~\ref{subfig:example_a} shows a collaboration social network $G$, which consists of 12 user vertices, $v_1 \sim v_{12}$, each with a set of skill labels (e.g., user $v_2$ has the ``back-end'' development skills), and collaborative edges (each connecting two users, e.g., $v_2$ and $v_3$, indicating that they collaborated on some project before). 
