The S$^3$AND problem has many other real applications. For example, in the Semantic Web applications~\cite{zheng2016semantic}, a SPARQL query can be considered as a query graph $q$ over a large knowledge graph $G$. Our S$^3$AND query can be used to return RDF subgraphs that follow the keyword constraints and have minor structural changes compared with $q$. 

