\section{Conclusions and future directions}
We proposed a new resource allocation and pricing mechanism based on an extended Fisher market model that accounts for external costs such as energy consumption and environmental impact. By incorporating Pigouvian taxes, our approach satisfies resource constraints towards sustainability while maximizing Nash welfare and proportional fairness among agents. We showed that the equilibrium problem can be solved using convex optimization, demonstrating the low complexity, practicality and effectiveness of our method.
