    % \end{equation}
    Specifically, while HTP prunes harmful tokens within layers $[ n ,  n + \Delta_n]$, BFR maintains a parallel branch that performs standard inference over the same layers and selectively restores benign features. This dual-path design enables the recovery of hidden states in subsequent layers, which are less susceptible to attack and primarily responsible for cross-modal integration and language refinement. By restoring previously pruned tokens at this stage, the model preserves functional performance without compromising safety. As shown in Eqn.~\ref{eqn:Benign_Features_Restoration_pipeline}:}
